  "why": "T-0543 exhausted the search INSIDE this deposit and was right: none of the 33 household continuation sheets among the 74 images foots printed 232. T-0736 went outside it by the second route that ticket named. The 1840 population schedules survive on NARA microfilm publication M704, and roll 57 is the one whose description reads \u201cColes, Cook, Crawford Counties\u201d; the Allen County Public Library Genealogy Center's scan of that roll is public and unauthenticated on the Internet Archive. Leaf n166 of it IS printed page 232 \u2014 identified by its own 31 heads of families, which are this page's 31 in this page's order, and not by the stamp alone \u2014 and leaf n167 is the facing right sheet of the same opening. It pairs on BOTH of T-0642's keys and on the sequence screen besides.",
